00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.030
SPEAKER: The Google
Cloud SDK, what is it?

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.040
The Google Cloud
Software Development Kit

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.570
is a collection
of tools that are

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.570
used to interact with Google
Cloud APIs and services

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:21.870
and manage the resources in
your Google Cloud projects.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.880
Together, these
tools help developers

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.070
and technical practitioners
be more efficient when

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.650
interacting with Google Cloud.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:32.549
The SDK includes the Google
Cloud CLI, Cloud Client

00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:37.150
Libraries, developer
tools and documentation.

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:39.060
The first piece of
the Google Cloud SDK

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.150
is the Google Cloud CLI, a
collection of command line

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:45.000
tools you can install to
access and manage your cloud

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.980
from the command line.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.110
With it, you can do
all kinds of things,

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:53.040
like manage virtual machines,
query Big Query tables,

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.110
update Google Cloud
storage buckets,

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:58.170
and virtually anything else you
can do in the Cloud Console,

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:01.920
all from your Linux,
MacOS or Windows terminal.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:05.040
Next in our SDK are
Cloud Client Libraries

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.020
for programmatically
integrating Google Cloud

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.120
APIs into your code.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.280
With high level
API abstractions,

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.010
Cloud Client Libraries handle
all the low level details

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.080
of communicating
with Google Cloud.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.270
This greatly reduces
the boilerplate code

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:19.770
you would have to
write otherwise

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.590
and lowers the learning curve so
you can hit the ground running

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:26.220
and start coding,
effectively and more quickly.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:29.010
Most importantly, Cloud
Client Libraries are available

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.800
for several programming
languages, including Java,

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:37.500
Python, Node.js, GO,
Ruby, C# and PHP.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.890
Each SDK will also have language
specific frameworks and tools

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:43.020
as available, so you'll
have everything you need,

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.570
no matter what your
favorite language is.

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:48.510
Cloud Client Libraries are
available for more than 100

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:50.010
Google Cloud Services.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.680
To help you better understand
how to best use them,

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.040
the Google Cloud SDK also
includes detailed documentation

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:59.190
that we've centralized on
cloud.google.com so you'll

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:02.550
always have access to
consistent, authoritative and

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:05.160
up-to-date technical reference
documentation and code

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.270
snippets.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:09.870
And finally, the SDK
optionally includes Cloud Code,

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:13.320
an ID extension available
for VS Code and IntelliJ that

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.480
helps you write,
debug and deploy

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.880
cloud native apps, all
without ever needing

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.010
to switch from your IDE window.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:23.190
Do you want to get started
using the Google Cloud SDK?

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.530
The Google Cloud CLI is
available via your operating

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:28.200
systems package manager
or a direct download

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.850
from cloud.google.com.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.380
And Cloud Client
Libraries can be

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.680
installed via standard library
package managers like npm

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.980
and pip, or via the language
specific Google Cloud Client

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:41.640
Libraries repositories linked in
the description of this video.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.710
To learn more about
the Google Cloud SDK,

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:45.958
check out cloud.google.com/sdk.

00:02:45.958 --> 00:02:49.140
[MUSIC PLAYING]

